  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0001] Raise BillingError with stable snake_case codes: Reject invalid input in ledgerly by raising BillingError(code, detail) with snake_case codes such as \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\" and \"negative_amount\"; reuse \"invalid_state\" with the message f\"invoice {invoice.id} is {invoice.status}\" for wrong-status checks, matching issue_invoice and payments.authorize.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0002] Normalize amounts with to_money and compare to ZERO: Convert any incoming amount through ledgerly.money.to_money before storing or comparing it, and compare against the ZERO constant rather than a literal Decimal; LineItem.unit_price must be a Decimal.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)\n- [at-0003] Reject bools when validating integer arguments: When validating an int argument such as quantity, exclude bool explicitly (isinstance(quantity, bool)) before the int check, since True/False pass isinstance(x, int).\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
